hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1130","Chapter on freeing captives without ransom, 1169 - Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had Mut'im ibn Adi, Abu Jubayr, been alive speaking to me concerning these filthy ones - meaning the captives of Badr - I would have released them to him. 1170 - Sufyan said once: Muhammad ibn Jubayr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [Flag: report 1170 is fragmentary in the printed text.]"
